{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"advisory":[{"agreement":1,"block_threshold":0.54,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Add a direct test of `has_atomic_basis` covering the False branches (non-PASS verdict, source!='attested', certifiable is False, missing/invalid completion_read_basis) and asserting each routes to the legacy path.","criteria":["tests"],"decision":"advisory","evidence":["src/rebar/_commands/completion_bundle.py:68 `def has_atomic_basis(result: Mapping[str, Any]) -> bool:` with conditions `result.get('source') == 'attested'` and `result.get('certifiable') is not False`","tests/interfaces/lifecycle/test_atomic_completion_close.py:67 `_atomic_pass` always sets `'source': 'attested'`, `'certifiable': True`, and a `completion_read_basis`","search for `has_atomic_basis` in tests returns no direct predicate test (only production references in close_precheck.py and completion_bundle.py)"],"finding":"The newly added eligibility predicate `has_atomic_basis` gates the entire atomic-vs-legacy close branch on four AND-ed conditions (verdict==PASS, source=='attested', certifiable is not False, completion_read_basis is a Mapping), but no test exercises its False branches. Every atomic-close test builds a fully eligible result via `_atomic_pass`, so the predicate always returns True; there is no test proving that a PASS with `certifiable: False` or `source: 'local'` (or a missing read basis) routes to the legacy close path instead of the atomic bundle.","id":"0","impact":0.45,"location":"src/rebar/_commands/completion_bundle.py:68","norm_id":"n7222802d969032b1","priority":0.3214,"reason":"default-advisory","reviewer_id":"code-review-tests","reviewers":["code-review-tests"],"scenarios":[],"severity":"minor","suggested_fix":"Add a table-driven unit test on `has_atomic_basis` with the four disqualifying inputs, plus a `_publish_close` test asserting the legacy `txn.transition_core` branch runs when `atomic_close is None`.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.7143,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"no","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"yes","path_reachable":"yes","respects_artifact_altitude":"na","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"blast_radius":"module","capability_degraded":false,"churn90":0,"contract_drift":false,"data_loss_without_recovery":false,"dead_code":false,"debt_impact":"medium","escapes_automation":true,"forbids_contract_allowed_state":false,"hard_to_reverse_surface":false,"hidden_invariant":false,"implicit_coupling":false,"likelihood":"low","prod_impact":"medium","reachable_path_without_automated_coverage":true,"removed_public_symbol":false,"reversibility":"easy","safety_net_removal_without_replacement":false,"security_bypass_not_enforced_elsewhere":false,"silent_failure":true,"silent_wrong_feeding_a_decision":false,"trigger_likelihood":"rare","unversioned_published_contract_break":false,"version_signal_present":false}}},{"agreement":1,"block_threshold":0.54,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Add a test that advances the CODE ref (or passes a `ref` resolving to a different SHA than `completion_read_basis.code_oid`) and asserts `commit_completion_bundle` raises the 'code ref changed' ConcurrencyMismatch without closing.","criteria":["tests"],"decision":"advisory","evidence":["src/rebar/_commands/completion_bundle.py:332 `if current != basis.code_oid.value: raise txn_concurrency_error('Error: code ref changed after completion verification; ...')`","search for `co