tract_break":false,"version_signal_present":false}}},{"agreement":1,"block_threshold":0.54,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Add a test that flips `sync.push` to `async` (or `off`) after `_atomic_pass` and asserts `commit_completion_bundle` aborts via the 'sync.push changed' ConcurrencyMismatch, leaving the ticket in_progress.","criteria":["tests"],"decision":"advisory","evidence":["src/rebar/_commands/completion_bundle.py:345 `if mode != 'always': raise txn_concurrency_error('Error: sync.push changed after the pinned completion run selected atomic delivery ...')`","src/rebar/_commands/completion_delivery.py:618 `if mode != 'always': raise _concurrency('Error: sync.push changed after the pinned completion run selected atomic delivery ...')`","search for `sync.push changed` in tests returns `(no matches)`","docs/concurrency.md added line: 'a mid-run policy change discards the private candidate and aborts'"],"finding":"The mid-run push-policy-change abort is documented as a hard contract ('a mid-run policy change discards the private candidate and aborts') but is untested. Neither `_require_atomic_delivery_mode` in `commit_completion_bundle` nor the `mode != 'always'` guard in `deliver_candidate` has a test asserting an atomic close aborts when `sync.push` is changed to `async`/`off` after the pinned run selected atomic delivery.","id":"2","impact":0.27,"location":"src/rebar/_commands/completion_bundle.py:339","norm_id":"na8a989e78bdb9fad","priority":0.2314,"reason":"default-advisory","reviewer_id":"code-review-tests","reviewers":["code-review-tests"],"scenarios":[],"severity":"minor","suggested_fix":"","tier":"LLM","validity":0.8571,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no